  {
   "text": "The knit vase is built as a single watertight body, 90 mm wide and 160 mm tall, with a 2 mm wall and a 2 mm floor. I haven't sliced or printed it.\n\nThe texture is a row of ridges running around the outside, with a 5 mm row pitch and 1.5 mm rib depth. It does not have the vertical columns of real knit stitches, so it reads as ribbed rather than knitted. Adding columns would mean many more features, so I kept it to one revolved profile.\n\nThe floor thickness, row pitch and rib depth were my guesses; you confirmed them on the sheet. The model is in the open project as \"Knit vase.\" Do you want me to slice it for the A1 mini, as selected, and queue it, or would you like to change the ribs first?"
  }
